  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. The period filter excluded usage at the exact start of the period, so the record at `start_ms` was dropped. I changed `start < ts < end` to `start <= ts < end`. The start is now inclusive and the end stays exclusive, so a record on a boundary lands in exactly one period.\n\nI did not add your reproduction test to the suite, so the 24 tests that passed are the existing ones. I did not run your reproduction on its own either.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
